==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|westen|wēsten|a desert, waste|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Germanic|wōstinnjō|a waste, wilderness|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|wāsto-|empty, wasted|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|fy|-}} {{term|woastyn||desert|lang=fy}}, {{etyl|frs|-}} {{term|wustenej||desert|lang=frs}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|woestijn||desert|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|gâtine||wasteland, moor|lang=fr}} ( < {{etyl|gem|-}}), {{etyl|gmh|-}} {{term|wuostinne||desert, wilderness|lang=gmh}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Wüste||desert|lang=de}}). More at {{l|en|westy}}, {{l|en|waste}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{obsolete}} A [[waste]], [[wasteland]]; [[desert]].

